---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';import {SITE} from '@/data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Academy4Tech" description="Learn about Academy4Tech, its practical engineering focus and founder Muhammed Nabeel.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'About'}]}/><div class="page-hero-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">The platform</div><h1>Built to share practical engineering knowledge.</h1><p>Academy4Tech is a personal, non-profit educational website created by Muhammed Nabeel for students, researchers, developers and people curious about robotics.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="article-shell" style="padding:0"><article class="article prose"><h2>About the author</h2><p>Muhammed Nabeel describes his work as centered on mechatronic systems, product development, prototyping and commissioning, with a particular interest in robotics and autonomous systems.</p><p>The profile on the original website records experience contributing to unmanned ground-vehicle platforms including SCORPIO-M and SCORPIO-S, mechatronic event systems including DNAxs and Sliding Screen, and Industrial Internet of Things and mobility prototypes. These details are preserved from the author's self-published profile and are not presented as independent third-party endorsements.</p><h2>Teaching approach</h2><p>The original Academy4Tech profile emphasizes a collaborative, inclusive relationship between educator and learner. The rebuilt platform continues that approach through open project records, practical sequences and clear links to source material.</p><h2>What Academy4Tech covers</h2><p>Core subjects include Python, IoT, Arduino, Raspberry Pi, C++, autonomous robotics, ROS, PCB design, Android interfaces, 3D modelling and printing, OpenCV, computer vision and machine learning.</p><h2 id="gallery">Legacy gallery record</h2><p>The former gallery named three events or collections: <strong>STEP 2020</strong>, <strong>GITEX 2019</strong> and <strong>Young Professionals in Space</strong>. The old images were not reused because they lacked alt text, source details and consistent presentation.</p></article><aside class="article-aside"><div class="toc"><h2>Connect</h2><ul><li><a href={SITE.social.linkedinOwner} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Muhammed Nabeel on LinkedIn</a></li><li><a href={SITE.social.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Academy4Tech on LinkedIn</a></li><li><a href={SITE.social.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tech2morrow on GitHub</a></li><li><a href={SITE.social.youtube} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Academy4Tech on YouTube</a></li><li><a href={`tel:${SITE.phone.replaceAll(' ','')}`}>{SITE.phone}</a></li></ul></div></aside></div></div></section>
  <section class="section surface-section"><div class="shell"><div class="cta-panel"><div><h2>Learn something. Build something. Share what worked.</h2><p>The platform is designed for a simple, transparent learning loop.</p></div><a class="button" href="/learn">Start learning</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
